What: phase-lock RAM KMS capture to the captured plane's CRTC vblank sequence.
Sample at capture_vblank_offset_ms (strict 0..1000 ms, default 0), validated
against physical refresh. Resynchronise missed refreshes; never drift or reuse a
sequence. Late entry waits for a future refresh. Timing fallback skips overdue
nominal deadlines. A call/sequence guard drops RT on missing pacing, re-reading or backwards sequence,
keeping RESET_ON_FORK. Failed demotion sleeps every refresh without acquisition.
No modesetting, affinity or scheduling authority is added.
Status: downstream ARM RAM KMS scheduling and safety correction.
Evidence: 2026-10-22 source-ID hunt: 135/4/0/38 misses; bad phases 2..5 ms,
clean 11..13 ms, nominal timer drift 2.27 ms/min; no scored CMA migrations.
Cost: vblank ioctls and phase latency; bounded driver waits and source-starvation
risk require real-device acceptance. Remove for equivalent upstream pacing.

